# Error pages + validation

Visitors, not engineers. Status pages + field errors stay plain English.

## Full-page errors (400s / 500s only)

No 2xx/3xx pages. Layout: one large `<h1>`, `max-w-3xl`, left, `<p>` body. No red text. No HTTP codes in UI (`404`, `500`, `Bad Request`). No humour (`Oops`). No blame. No vague “technical difficulties”.

`<title>`: `{H1} – CHSTR Run & Social`.

Always say next step. **Back** (history) and **Home** `/`. Contact `/contact`.

| Case | H1 | Body |
|---|---|---|
| Missing URL | `Page not found` | Typed address: check it. Pasted: copy the whole address. Still wrong: home or contact. |
| Unexpected failure | `Sorry, there is a problem with the site` | Try again later. Basket is saved on this device. Contact us if you need help now. |
| Checkout cancelled | `Your payment was not taken` | Basket is still saved. Back to basket. |

## Validation + inline errors

Human line first. What to do, not what broke. Provider / Zod JSON / stack / HTTP codes never shown.

- Fields: destructive-token text beside the field. Zod `error` messages set per schema — never default “Too small: expected…”.
- Persist raw error in logs if needed. Present a human line at the UI.
